quest.signalindustries.welcome.name=Welcome!
quest.signalindustries.welcome.desc=Welcome to Signal Industries!\nSI is a technomagical mod with many machines and gadgets split between 4 tiers.\n\nEach tier has a dedicated chapter in the questbook.\n\nThis quest book isn't finished yet, but in the future it should contain enough information to progress through the entirety of the mod.\n\nTry holding CTRL while hovering over items, SI uses BTA descriptions to provide more info about blocks and items.\n\nDon't forget to check the guidebook by pressing [R], all recipes and more are there!
quest.signalindustries.genesis.name=Genesis
quest.signalindustries.genesis.desc=Your first task is finding a meteor containing a red ore that you will need a diamond pickaxe to mine, this will be the main resource of this mod.\n\nMeteors spawn randomly in the world and can be of 3 types:\n- Iron\n- Signalite\n- Dilithium\n\nYou don't need to worry about the last one for now.\n\nLater on you will be able to craft a special compass that will point you to the closest meteor.
quest.signalindustries.tome.name=Unused
quest.signalindustries.tome.desc=This entry is currently unused, but might be used again in the future.
quest.signalindustries.hammer.name=Hammer Time!
quest.signalindustries.hammer.desc=Use a hammer crafted out of some iron and sticks, it will allow you to make plates out of the most basic materials.
quest.signalindustries.cobblePlates.name=Cobblestone Plates
quest.signalindustries.cobblePlates.desc=Turn your cobblestone into plates using the <Plate Hammer>.
quest.signalindustries.stonePlates.name=Stone Plates
quest.signalindustries.stonePlates.desc=Turn your stone into plates using the <Plate Hammer>.
quest.signalindustries.prototypeCore.name=Prototype Machine Core
quest.signalindustries.prototypeCore.desc=Combine your 2 types of plates and a <Raw Signalite Crystal> to make the core for the first tier of machines.
quest.signalindustries.prototypeAlloySmelter.name=Prototype Alloy Smelter
quest.signalindustries.prototypeAlloySmelter.desc=Combines materials to make new materials, can make <Steel> more efficiently.
quest.signalindustries.prototypeCrusher.name=Prototype Crusher
quest.signalindustries.prototypeCrusher.desc=Crushes items into dusts.
quest.signalindustries.diamondGear.name=Diamond Cutting Gear
quest.signalindustries.diamondGear.desc=A sharp diamond gear that can be used to cut other crystals or other materials.
quest.signalindustries.prototypeCrystalCutter.name=Prototype Crystal Cutter
quest.signalindustries.prototypeCrystalCutter.desc=Cuts materials using a sharp diamond gear. Used primarily to make <Signalite Crystals> out of <Raw S. Crystals>.
quest.signalindustries.prototypeExtractor.name=Prototype Signalite Extractor
quest.signalindustries.prototypeExtractor.desc=This is the first machine you should make, it allows you to burn any furnace combustible fuel along with <Raw S. Crystal> to gain <Signaling Energy>.
quest.signalindustries.prototypePlateFormer.name=Prototype Plate Former
quest.signalindustries.prototypePlateFormer.desc=Makes plates out of various materials, higher yield for <Cobblestone & Stone Plates>, required for plates made out of more advanced materials.
quest.signalindustries.crystal.name=Signalite Crystal
quest.signalindustries.crystal.desc=A bright red crystal with enormous power, used as a crafting ingredient in many recipes. You will need one for the next tier of <Machine Core>.
quest.signalindustries.crystalBattery.name=Signalite Crystal (Battery)
quest.signalindustries.crystalBattery.desc=This is a modified crystal that can store and release <S. Energy>. Simply click with it in on any slot that contains or accepts <S. Energy>.
quest.signalindustries.energy.name=Signaling Energy
quest.signalindustries.energy.desc=This is the power source for all machines and gadgets in Signal Industries.\n\nGained from extracting <Raw S. Crystals> in an <Extractor>, or later on collected passively from the air.\n\nCan be transported either by conduits designed for it or by a crystal battery\n\nIn theory works by converting one type of energy to another when excited by an outside signal.\n\n<Signalite Crystals> are therefore special because of their ability to protect this energy from outside influence until it is needed.
quest.signalindustries.energyCell.name=Prototype Energy Cell
quest.signalindustries.energyCell.desc=This block can store a fair amount of <S. Energy>. The energy will be released (lost) when this block is broken, so be careful.
quest.signalindustries.energyConduit.name=Prototype Signalum Conduit
quest.signalindustries.energyConduit.desc=Transfers <Signaling Energy>, usually tries to balance out its contents across the whole pipe line. Contents are lost when the conduit is broken.
quest.signalindustries.fluidConduit.name=Prototype Fluid Conduit
quest.signalindustries.fluidConduit.desc=Transfers any other fluid apart from <Signaling Energy>, usually tries to balance out its contents across the whole pipe line. Contents are lost when the conduit is broken.
quest.signalindustries.fluidTank.name=Prototype Fluid Tank
quest.signalindustries.fluidTank.desc=Can store a few buckets of one type of fluid. Contents are *preserved* when this block is broken, allowing it to also function as basically a bigger bucket. Can interact with fluid slots.
quest.signalindustries.inserter.name=Prototype Inserter
quest.signalindustries.inserter.desc=Either grabs the first available item of an inventory or picks up items from the ground and pushes them into an <Item Conduit>.
quest.signalindustries.ioConfig.name=I/O Configuration
quest.signalindustries.ioConfig.desc=Almost every machines has a [I] and/or a [F] button in its GUI. Clicking them will open their respective I/O configuration screens for the machine.\n\nIn the config screens, buttons over the "I/O" text control the access to that side of a block:\n[I] means input.\n[O] means output.\n[B] means both.\n[X] means none.\n\nButtons over the "Slot" text configure which item or fluid slot of the block will be used for that side of the machine.
quest.signalindustries.itemConduit.name=Prototype Item Conduit
quest.signalindustries.itemConduit.desc=Transfers any block or item slowly. Contents will drop onto the ground if broken or if there isn't a valid destination for them.\n\nItem conduits automatically pick up items from properly configured SI machines, for other inventories use an <Inserter> or the <External I/O> machine.
quest.signalindustries.pump.name=Prototype Pump
quest.signalindustries.pump.desc=Extracts water from the world, use <Fluid Conduits>, <Fluid Tanks) and proper I/O configuration to get it out.
quest.signalindustries.storageContainer.name=Prototype Storage Container
quest.signalindustries.storageContainer.desc=Holds 4096 (64 stacks) of a single type of item. Right-click to insert items and left-click to extract.
quest.signalindustries.tablet.name=Configuration Tablet
quest.signalindustries.tablet.desc=A handy multi-tool for manipulating with machines, it can rotate machines, configure their I/O or covers and disconnect pipes or covers from machines.\n\nModes can be switched with Shift + Right Mouse Button.\n\nWhen hovering over a machine with this in your hand, the outline box will be split into several sections, clicking on a corner will interact with the opposite side.
quest.signalindustries.emptyCrystal.name=Empty Crystals
quest.signalindustries.emptyCrystal.desc=The <Crystal Cutter> can process the same input into several different outputs depending on the ID set in it's UI.\n\nThe correct IDs for <Crystal Cutter> recipes can always be found in the guidebook.\n\nThese will be a very important ingredient in the Basic tier but will need to be processed several times.
quest.signalindustries.steel.name=Steel
quest.signalindustries.steel.desc=This is a material from BTA itself and also a big component for the Basic-tier.\n\nLater on there will be a cheaper recipe for it using SI machines.
quest.signalindustries.crystalDust.name=Empty Crystal Dust
quest.signalindustries.crystalDust.desc=Crushing <Empty S. Crystals> inside a <Crusher> yields, unsurprisingly, empty crystal dust.
quest.signalindustries.crystalAlloy.name=Crystal Alloy
quest.signalindustries.crystalAlloy.desc=An alloy of steel and empty crystal dust, this is the primary material of the Basic tier.
quest.signalindustries.crystalAlloyPlates.name=Crystal Alloy Plates
quest.signalindustries.crystalAlloyPlates.desc=Crystal Alloy ingots pressed inside of a <Plate Former>.
quest.signalindustries.meteorCompass.name=Meteor Tracker
quest.signalindustries.meteorCompass.desc=This handy tool will point you to the closes meteor, making them a lot easier to find!\n\nRight-click for the first time to calibrate and any right-click after that to get more precise information.\n\nTo stop tracking an already mined out meteor for example, you can shift+right-click near it.
quest.signalindustries.steelPlates.name=Steel Plates
quest.signalindustries.steelPlates.desc=Steel ingots pressed inside of a <Plate Former>.
quest.signalindustries.basicCore.name=Basic Machine Core
quest.signalindustries.basicCore.desc=The main component of every Basic-tier machine.
quest.signalindustries.basicExtractor.name=Basic Signalite Extractor
quest.signalindustries.basicExtractor.desc=This is a proper version of the <Signalite Extractor>, extracts more energy per crystal than the Prototype variant.
quest.signalindustries.basicCollector.name=Basic Signalite Collector
quest.signalindustries.basicCollector.desc=Using the meshes you made, you can craft an alternative to extractors, using a <S. Crystal> as a catalyst, this machine can passively pull in lingering <S. Energy> from the air slowly.\n\nWorks better near fallen <Signalite Ore Meteors>.
quest.signalindustries.basicCrusher.name=Basic Crusher
quest.signalindustries.basicCrusher.desc=This is a proper version of the <Crusher>.\n\nYields more dusts from crystals.\n\nAlso allows you to double your yield of iron and gold from ore by turning 1 ore into 2 dusts which then can be each smelted into ingots.
quest.signalindustries.netherCoalDust.name=Nether Coal Dust
quest.signalindustries.netherCoalDust.desc=BTAs nether coal can be crushed down into a dust to create new materials or cheaper steel if crushed again.
quest.signalindustries.cheaperSteel.name=Cheaper Steel
quest.signalindustries.cheaperSteel.desc=Crushing <Nether CoaL> twice will grant you tiny nether coal dusts, these can be used with iron ingots inside of an <Alloy Smelter> to create steel more easily.
quest.signalindustries.basicSmelter.name=Basic Alloy Smelter
quest.signalindustries.basicSmelter.desc=This is a proper version of the <Alloy Smelter>.\n\nYields 2x as much crystal alloy than the Prototype variant and unlocks creating a new type of alloy.
quest.signalindustries.basicInfuser.name=Basic Infuser
quest.signalindustries.basicInfuser.desc=A new type of machine that infuses one material into another. One input can be a fluid.
quest.signalindustries.basicCutter.name=Basic Crystal Cutter
quest.signalindustries.basicCutter.desc=This is a proper version of the <Crystal Cutter>.\n\nCan carry out crystal cutting recipes with only half the required amount of materials compared to the Prototype variant.
quest.signalindustries.basicPress.name=Basic Metal Press
quest.signalindustries.basicPress.desc=This is a proper version of the <Plate Former>.\n\nCan make plates out of more complex materials.
quest.signalindustries.saturatedAlloy.name=Saturated Alloy Ingots
quest.signalindustries.saturatedAlloy.desc=Infusing crystal alloy with signalite dust creates this saturated alloy. Useful later on.
quest.signalindustries.saturatedAlloyPlate.name=Saturated Alloy Plates
quest.signalindustries.saturatedAlloyPlate.desc=As with most materials you can make it into a plate.
quest.signalindustries.signalumAlloyMesh.name=Signalite Alloy Mesh
quest.signalindustries.signalumAlloyMesh.desc=A thin plate of <Signalite Alloy> with holes cut into it. Used in the making of a certain machine.
quest.signalindustries.basicChamber.name=Basic Crystallizer
quest.signalindustries.basicChamber.desc=Allows you to combine crystal batteries together to increase their size and therefore capacity.
quest.signalindustries.basicAutoMiner.name=Basic Automatic Miner
quest.signalindustries.basicAutoMiner.desc=This machine allows you to automatically dig for resources when provided with <S. Energy>.\n\nThe area of operation is highlighted with an orange box and extends all the way down to bedrock.\n\nMined blocks are usually outputted from the top of the machine, you can use a chest, item conduit or basket to collect them (don't forget to configure the I/O properly using the [I] button).
quest.signalindustries.precisionChip.name=Silk Touch Mining
quest.signalindustries.precisionChip.desc=When inserted allows an <Automatic Miner> to dig blocks as if it had silk touch at the cost of higher energy usage, also increases the time it takes a mine a block.
quest.signalindustries.basicAssembler.name=Basic Assembler
quest.signalindustries.basicAssembler.desc=An automatic crafting table, set up a crafting template in it's UI and then it use items from its inventory to repeatedly craft that item.
quest.signalindustries.basicCatalystConduit.name=Basic Universal Energy Conduit
quest.signalindustries.basicCatalystConduit.desc=Transfers energy that might be used by other mods.
quest.signalindustries.basicChip.name=Crystal Chip
quest.signalindustries.basicChip.desc=A chip cut from a <Raw Signalite Crystal> using a <Crystal Cutter>.
quest.signalindustries.basicContainer.name=Basic Storage Container
quest.signalindustries.basicContainer.desc=A bigger container that holds 8192 (128 stacks) of a single type of item. Right-click to insert items and left-click to extract.
quest.signalindustries.basicDynamo.name=Basic Signalite Dynamo
quest.signalindustries.basicDynamo.desc=Uses <Signaling Energy> to create a different form of energy that other mods can use.
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyCell.name=Basic Energy Cell
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyCell.desc=A bigger container for <Signaling Energy>.
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyConduit.name=Basic Signalum Conduit
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyConduit.desc=Transfers <Signaling Energy> at a faster rate.
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyCore.name=Basic Energy Core
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyCore.desc=This core is a component in more complex Basic-tier machines.
quest.signalindustries.redstoneBooster.name=Redstone Booster
quest.signalindustries.redstoneBooster.desc=This machine can boost the processing speed of another machine slightly by using redstone.\n\nThe correct side has to be pointing towards and adjacent to the machine to be boosted.
quest.signalindustries.basicFluidConduit.name=Basic Fluid Conduit
quest.signalindustries.basicFluidConduit.desc=Transfers fluid at a faster rate.
quest.signalindustries.basicFluidTank.name=Basic Fluid Tank
quest.signalindustries.basicFluidTank.desc=A bigger container for any fluid.
quest.signalindustries.basicInserter.name=Basic Inserter
quest.signalindustries.basicInserter.desc=Grabs several items either from the ground or a connected inventory and pushes them into an <Item Conduit>.
quest.signalindustries.basicItemConduit.name=Basic Item Conduit
quest.signalindustries.basicItemConduit.desc=A faster <Item Conduit>.
quest.signalindustries.basicRestrictItemConduit.name=Basic Restrict Item Conduit
quest.signalindustries.basicRestrictItemConduit.desc=A special type of <Item Conduit> that can have any of its sides blocked, items will not be able to exit the conduit in blocked direction but they can still enter.
quest.signalindustries.basicSensorItemConduit.name=Basic Sensor Item Conduit
quest.signalindustries.basicSensorItemConduit.desc=A special type of <Item Conduit> that sends out a redstone signal if a specific item and amount are travelling through it.
quest.signalindustries.basicInjector.name=Basic Energy Injector
quest.signalindustries.basicInjector.desc=This machine can recharge some of your gadgets that use <S. Energy>.
quest.signalindustries.covers.name=Covers
quest.signalindustries.covers.desc=Covers are items that can be attached to sides of machines for extended functionality.\n\nThey can be configured further or removed using a <Configuration Tablet>.
quest.signalindustries.conveyorCover.name=Conveyor Cover
quest.signalindustries.conveyorCover.desc=This cover can transport items directly to another block.
quest.signalindustries.pumpCover.name=Pump Cover
quest.signalindustries.pumpCover.desc=This cover can directly transport fluids to another block.
quest.signalindustries.redstoneCover.name=Redstone Cover
quest.signalindustries.redstoneCover.desc=This cover can make a machine output a redstone signal depending on a set condition (Currently unfinished, doesn't work)
quest.signalindustries.switchCover.name=Switch Cover
quest.signalindustries.switchCover.desc=This cover can disable a machine from working.
quest.signalindustries.voidCover.name=Void Cover
quest.signalindustries.voidCover.desc=This cover DESTROYS any fluid or item in a configured slots when active.
quest.signalindustries.glowingObsidian.name=Glowing Obsidian
quest.signalindustries.glowingObsidian.desc=Infusing obsidian with molten rock and nether coal dust results in a super tough, super heat-resistant glowing material.\n\nYou will take great advantage of this soon...
quest.signalindustries.romChips.name=Ability ROM Chips
quest.signalindustries.romChips.desc=Contain code for various abilities that a <Signalum Power Harness> can use, can be found in dungeons and labyrinths.
quest.signalindustries.triggers.name=Triggers
quest.signalindustries.triggers.desc=Triggers are used to activate <S. Power Harness> abilities, but they first need to be programmed inside an <EEPROM Programmer> using code found in <ROM Chips>.\n\nA programmed trigger will have all its important information written in its tooltip and can be activated when held with a right click!
quest.signalindustries.powerHarness.name=Signalum Power Harness
quest.signalindustries.powerHarness.desc=A harness you can equip to use various abilities provided by <Triggers>.\n\nShift right click with it in your hand to access its internal energy storage.\n\nEquipping the goggles also allows you to see more information about currently equipped gadgets.
quest.signalindustries.basicDrill.name=Basic Signalite Drill
quest.signalindustries.basicDrill.desc=This is basically a signalite powered pickaxe, can be charged inside of an <Energy Injector>.\n\nYou will need a few additional parts to assemble it.
quest.signalindustries.basicCasing.name=Basic Casing
quest.signalindustries.basicCasing.desc=Standard casing made out of <Crystal Alloy>, Basic-tier multiblocks are usually made primarily out of this.
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyConnector.name=Basic Energy Connector
quest.signalindustries.basicEnergyConnector.desc=A Basic-tier energy plug for multiblocks. The entire structure draws <Signaling Energy> from this block.
quest.signalindustries.basicInductionSmelter.name=Basic Induction Smelter
quest.signalindustries.basicInductionSmelter.desc=Probably your first multiblock!\n\nThis is a bigger furnace that always smelts 16 items at all at once using <S. Energy>.\n\nPlacing down this controller block will visualize a hologram of the required structure around it.\n\nAlternatively, you can look inside the guidebook for both on how to build the multiblock and its material costs.
quest.signalindustries.basicItemInput.name=Basic Item Input Bus
quest.signalindustries.basicItemInput.desc=A 4 slot item input for multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.basicItemOutput.name=Basic Item Output Bus
quest.signalindustries.basicItemOutput.desc=A 4 slot item output for multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.signaliteAlloyCoil.name=Saturated Signalite Alloy Coil
quest.signalindustries.signaliteAlloyCoil.desc=A coil of saturated signalite alloy wrapped around a rod of unsaturated <Crystal Alloy>. Used in multiblocks mainly as a heating component.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedAlloy.name=Reinforced Crystal Alloy Ingot
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedAlloy.desc=Combining <Crystal Alloy> with <Glowing Obsidian> creates a super strong dark alloy. It is the basis of the Reinforced tier.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedAlloyPlates.name=Reinforced Crystal Alloy Plate
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedAlloyPlates.desc=Plates made out of <R.C. Alloy>, used in probably every Reinforced-tier machine or gadget.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCore.name=Reinforced Machine Core
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCore.desc=The chassis of Reinforced-tier machines.
quest.signalindustries.dilithiumOre.name=Dilithium Ore
quest.signalindustries.dilithiumOre.desc=Shards of this extraterrestrial ore can create a field around them where the passage of time is noticeably accelerated when excited by, for example, <Signaling Energy>.\n\nSadly, it looks like inducing this effect degrades this material to nothing over time.
quest.signalindustries.pureChip.name=Pure Crystal Chip
quest.signalindustries.pureChip.desc=A cutout piece of a <Signalite Crystal>, this one has been cut to higher standards.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCutter.name=Reinforced Crystal Cutter
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCutter.desc=An upgraded <Crystal Cutter> that cut more exotic materials, can also make chips out of <Signalite Crystals> more precisely making <Pure Crystal Chips>.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedDrill.name=Reinforced Signalite Drill
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedDrill.desc=An upgraded version of the Signalite Drill, can mine a larger area at once using the [Change Mode] keybind.\n\nIt is also necessary for mining out <Dilithium> and <Dimensional Shards>.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedEnergyCore.name=Reinforced Energy Core
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedEnergyCore.desc=This core is a component in more complex Reinforced-tier machines.
quest.signalindustries.signaliteGear.name=Signalite Cutting Gear
quest.signalindustries.signaliteGear.desc=A sharper and tougher gear made out of <Signalite Crystals> for cutting more exotic materials.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedTracker.name=Reinforced Meteor Tracker
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedTracker.desc=This advanced tracker can pick up the faint presence of <Signalite> deep underground, while the vertical range is impressive this causes the horizontal range to be limited.\n\nAs such this tracker can only scan for <Signalite> presence in a 3x3 block radius.\n\nAdditionally, a certain anomalous structure seems to interfere with the scanning process.
quest.signalindustries.dilithiumPlate.name=Dilithium Plate
quest.signalindustries.dilithiumPlate.desc=Plates made out of <Dilithium> are used in specialized machines that make use of its signature ability.
quest.signalindustries.blueprint.name=Blueprint
quest.signalindustries.blueprint.desc=A blueprint of some multiblock structure.\n\nShift right click on a multiblock controller to write its structure unto the blueprint.
quest.signalindustries.builder.name=Reinforced Builder
quest.signalindustries.builder.desc=Can automatically built structures from blueprints, you can also set the rotation and offset where the structure will be placed.\n\nAll required building materials need placed into the machines inventory.
quest.signalindustries.dimensionalOre.name=Dimensional Shard Ore
quest.signalindustries.dimensionalOre.desc=Odd structures of unknown purpose have begun showing up in the overworld.\n\nIn their center is a tall rod, and in the very center of that rod is a piece of crystallized reality.\n\nThese shards are theorized to be able to manipulate space in unique ways due to their underlying link to dimensions.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCasing.name=Reinforced Casing
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCasing.desc=Tougher casing made out of <R. C. Alloy>, Reinforced-tier multiblocks are usually made primarily out of this.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCasing2.name=Reinforced Casing (Type 2)
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedCasing2.desc=An alternate casing used in some Reinforced-tier multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedEnergyConnector.name=Reinforced Energy Connector
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedEnergyConnector.desc=A Reinforced-tier energy plug for multiblocks. The entire structure draws <Signaling Energy> from this block.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedFluidInput.name=Reinforced Fluid Input Hatch
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedFluidInput.desc=A fluid input hatch for multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedFluidOutput.name=Reinforced Fluid Output Hatch
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedFluidOutput.desc=A fluid output hatch for multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedGrating.name=Reinforced Grate
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedGrating.desc=An grate of <Signalite Alloy Mesh> and <R. C. Alloy> used in some Reinforced-tier multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedItemInput.name=Reinforced Item Input Bus
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedItemInput.desc=A 9 slot item input for multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedItemOutput.name=Reinforced Item Output Bus
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedItemOutput.desc=A 9 slot item input for multiblocks.
quest.signalindustries.warpOrb.name=Warp Orb
quest.signalindustries.warpOrb.desc=Can be encoded with a specific position in space using a special machine.\n\nCan also be broken by a sufficiently powerful gadget, leading to a temporary rip in spacetime that effectively teleports anyone near to the location encoded in the orb.\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is not recommended to break one with no location encoded unless you're sufficiently prepared.
quest.signalindustries.booster.name=Dilithium Booster
quest.signalindustries.booster.desc=A specialized machine utilizing the signature property of <Dilithium>, it speeds up some other machine adjacent to it.\n\nThe correct side has to be facing the machine.
quest.signalindustries.eclipse.name=Eclipse
quest.signalindustries.eclipse.desc=Once a year, the moon covers the sun, and the Eclipse begins. A special kind of fiery monster comes out of hiding for this occasion.
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedWrathBeacon.name=Reinforced Wrath Beacon
quest.signalindustries.reinforcedWrathBeacon.desc=The Ashen Trees hold a malicious secret that can only be discovered through this machine.\n\nWhen the correct structure is made and an <Infernal Eye> is offered, begins the Reinforced-tier Wrath Beacon challenge.\n\nChallenge consists of several waves of monsters that you must fight through.\n\nThe reward is a key to your future.
quest.signalindustries.anchor.name=Dimensional Anchor
quest.signalindustries.anchor.desc=A multiblock designed for encoding a location onto a <Warp Orb> placed inside.\n\nAll 4 stabilizers need to be fueled (by Dilithium Shards) and powered (by Signaling Energy) through the entire encoding process.\n\nEncoding a blank <Warp Orb> takes several minutes.
quest.signalindustries.dilithiumChip.name=Dilithium Chip
quest.signalindustries.dilithiumChip.desc=A cutout piece of a <Dilithium Shard>. Used in a specific circuit making use of the minerals special properties.
quest.signalindustries.dimensionalChip.name=Dimensional Chip
quest.signalindustries.dimensionalChip.desc=A cutout piece of a <Dimensional Shard>. Used in a specific circuit making use of the minerals special properties.
quest.signalindustries.eternity.name=Eternity
quest.signalindustries.eternity.desc=The foundation of reality, connected to all other dimensions, filling the space between them. Surprisingly not empty, but is instead filled with odd wonders and rare resources.
quest.signalindustries.pulsarBlock.name=The Pulsar
quest.signalindustries.pulsarBlock.desc=A machine capable of unleashing a large shockwave of <Signaling Energy>, dealing massive AOE damage to nearby enemies.\n\nAlternatively, can focus its stored energy into a singular point in its center where an item can also be slotted in.\n\nTo mind comes a particular orb that might need this kind and amount of force to "open".\n\nCan be activated remotely via redstone.
quest.signalindustries.pulsar.name=The Pulsar (Portable)
quest.signalindustries.pulsar.desc=A portable, item form of the <Pulsar>, weaker than the block counterpart but can still do the same stuff.
quest.signalindustries.pulsarAttachment.name=The Pulsar (Attachment)
quest.signalindustries.pulsarAttachment.desc=This is an attachment version of the portable <Pulsar> that can be connected to a <Signalum Power Suit>.\n\nAlt+Keybind to open inventory.\nShift+Keybind to charge.\nKeybind to activate.
quest.signalindustries.signalumSaber.name=Signalite Saber
quest.signalindustries.signalumSaber.desc=A sword whose blade is maintained by <Signaling Energy>.\n\nAs such has to be powered to be effective, but can inflict severe damage if so.
quest.signalindustries.powerSuit.name=Signalum Power Suit
quest.signalindustries.powerSuit.desc=<todo>
quest.signalindustries.saturatedKey.name=Saturated Key
quest.signalindustries.saturatedKey.desc=The reward for completing the Reinforced Wrath Beacon challenge.\n\nA literal and metaphorical key for reaching new heights.
quest.signalindustries.stabilizer.name=Dilithium Stabilizer
quest.signalindustries.stabilizer.desc=This machine is the inverse to the <Dilithium Booster>, used in some multiblocks to stabilize some kind of action by locally slowing down time instead.
quest.signalindustries.reactor.name=Signalite Reactor
quest.signalindustries.reactor.desc=Remember that you can check the vanilla BTA guidebook for the resources required to build any multiblock!\n\nOne of the more important multiblocks, facilitates a special reaction between <Signaling Energy>, pushing its conversion ability to the extremes.\n\nThis reaction is crude and most of the energy will end up into a permanent low-energy state which will not respond to any more signals.\n\nBut a small amount of it might manage to go beyond its limits.

